// Type-checking for scripts/, which svelte-check does not cover.
//
// The root tsconfig.json covers src and the vite config, as SvelteKit 2's
// generated config did — and under that generated list scripts/run-pipeline.ts,
// the ingestion pipeline that runs in production every 15 minutes, had ZERO type
// coverage in CI. It could have been broken by any change to src/lib/server/*
// and nothing would have said so until a scheduled run failed.
//
// This is a SEPARATE project rather than more `include` on the root on purpose.
// Scripts run under tsx as plain Node, so they get Node's types and not
// SvelteKit's: a `$app/*` import (in a script, or in a src/lib/server module one
// loads) exists only inside a Vite build, and fails here rather than in a
// scheduled run. This repo has already been bitten three times by configuration
// that quietly did nothing (duplicate migration versions making `supabase db
// reset` a no-op, the generated include above, and sharp's exports map hiding
// its own types); one source of truth per scope is cheaper than a fourth.
//
// compilerOptions are inherited from the root config so the two agree on
// strictness. Only the file set and types differ. Scripts import from src/ with
// relative paths and use no #lib alias, so nothing else is needed.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts"]
}
